cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fastpostgres in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "FastPostgres: PostgreSQL query results over POSIX shared memory"
abstract: >-
  fastpostgres delivers PostgreSQL query results through POSIX shared memory as
  typed arrays instead of the socket's text protocol: a background worker
  publishes each batch in /dev/shm - the executor's own tuple bytes (FPROWS) or
  a columnar frame (FPCOLUMN) - and the Python client reads them in place.
  Measured against ADBC + Arrow on the same rows, it returns Python tuples
  5.0-5.7x faster and consumes columnar results 3.6-3.8x faster; the row decode
  itself runs at ~725 instructions per row with ~10 branch mispredictions.
type: software
authors:
